        "id": 16902,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-24T23:48:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, all the Innate powers have &nbsp;multiple options, with different elemental needs. Are these exclusive of each other?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I believe, with the 'Do as Much as you can' rule, that you do all that you can, and some of them that say 'Instead', are obvious - usually thats modifying the first level of the power.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But like, Sharp Fangs Behind the LEaves Raging hunt, I believe that means I can Gather 1 (Beast) and Push 2 (Beast) automatically from the same target land (should I want) - and if I happen to have the 2 plant, i can also do the damage? So I could, theortically, Gather 1 Beast into a land, have, say 3 Beast there and do 3 Damage, then push 2 of them out somewhere else?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sharp Fangs is good for a second question - Do you have to do them in order, or could I Push 2 then do the the damage (which would be less I know, but might be useful in saving a Beast Token from being destroyed by it destroying a city/town) and then gather 1 of them back?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:49:47.437Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 133,
